In this NWSS R Study Hall presentation, we, Rebecca Schneider and Jose Palacio, share practical methods for analyzing and visualizing wastewater surveillance data in R. Using synthetic weekly data, we demonstrate how to estimate underlying trends through natural cubic spline smoothing and state-space modeling with Kalman filtering. We also explain how to handle non-detects and create base R plots that clearly display trend estimates, uncertainty bands, detection limits, and missing observations.
